Copyright (c) 2026 Isabella du Preez. All rights reserved.

## Overview

This is a proprietary license for early-stage personal projects. It's designed to be straightforward, casual, and legally protective without corporate jargon. This license gives me (the copyright holder) control over my work while I decide what direction it should take long-term — whether that's open-source, commercial, GPL, or something else entirely.

## Scope: What This License Covers

Everything in this repository is covered by this license, including but not limited to:

- **Source code** (scripts, programs, applications, libraries)
- **Creative assets** (art, designs, graphics, animations, audio, video)
- **Machine learning models** (trained models, weights, datasets, training code)
- **Documentation** (READMEs, wikis, guides, comments, technical notes)
- **Configuration files** (build scripts, deployment configs, CI/CD pipelines)
- **Project-specific integrations** (custom modifications, patches, customizations)
- **Any other original work** created, written, or substantially modified by Isabella du Preez

In short: if I made it or significantly altered it, it's covered by this license.

## What You Can Do

**Personal use only.** You may clone, download, and use this repository privately for personal learning, reference, or development purposes. You may run the code, read the documentation, study the implementation, and experiment locally on your own machine.

**Respect third-party licenses.** Any open-source components, freely licensed libraries, or openly licensed assets used in this project (such as the Godot engine, FOSS libraries, or CC-licensed artwork) remain governed by their original licenses and are **not** restricted by this file. You are free to use, redistribute, or modify those third-party components according to their respective licenses.

## What You Cannot Do

You do **not** have permission to:

- **Copy, duplicate, or clone** this repository for distribution or storage (except for your personal use)
- **Modify or create derivative works** from my original code or assets for any purpose other than private experimentation
- **Redistribute, publish, or release** any part of this project publicly (on GitHub, package managers, asset stores, forums, etc.)
- **Use this code or assets commercially** (sell it, incorporate it into commercial products, monetize it, etc.) without explicit written permission
- **Train AI models or language models** on this code, documentation, or assets, or use this project as training data without explicit written permission
- **Fork this repository** publicly or create competing versions
- **Sublicense, relicense, or transfer rights** to anyone else

If you do any of these things, you're infringing on my copyright.

## What This Means for Contributors

If you'd like to **contribute, collaborate, or request permission** to use any part of this project, get in touch. I'm open to conversations about:

- **Collaboration** on development
- **Contributions** to the project
- **Licensing exceptions** for specific use cases
- **Commercial use** agreements
- **Open-sourcing or relicensing** parts of the project

Contact me at: **visrali@disroot.org**
## Future Licensing

I reserve the right to **relicense, open-source, or release** parts (or all) of this project under different terms at any point in the future. When that happens, I'll make it clear which parts are affected and under what license(s) they're available. Until then, this license applies.

For some of my projects, I fully plan to eventually switch to **GPL**, **MIT**, **CC0**, or other open-source/copyleft licenses. This license is a temporary measure for early-stage work.

## Important Notes

- **This is not legal advice.** This license is a practical, friendly placeholder. If you need a formally binding, legally detailed license or contributor agreements later, consult a lawyer.
- **I'm not trying to gatekeep open source.** I love open-source software and contribute to it. This license just lets me protect my work while I'm figuring out what I want to do with it long-term.
- **AI training and scraping.** Please do not use this code or documentation to train machine learning models, language models, or AI systems without permission. This is especially important as AI training datasets become more common.

## Updates and Changes

I may update the copyright holder name, contact details, or this license text as needed. The version number will increment with significant changes (e.g., v1.1.0, v2.0.0).

